# Repos the indexer suite needs checked out BESIDE it on the CI venue.
#
# Declaring a sibling here is what makes its cross-repo guards actually run. An
# UNdeclared sibling is not a neutral omission: every guard written against it
# resolves with existsSync, calls this.skip(), and the gate still prints PASS,
# so the run reports green having exercised none of them. Measured 2026-08-12
# across the nine gated repos, this was the ONE whose roster was already
# complete, so its venue counts already equal a full local checkout's. See
# test/unit/sibling-coverage.test.js, which reports the surface this file leaves
# uncovered and now fails if a guard's sibling is ever added without a line here.
#
# ci-dispatch.sh ships each of these at its origin/master (falling back to local
# HEAD) and REFUSES the push if one is not a checkout beside this repo, so a
# declared sibling can never be silently absent.

# Vendored coins-registry byte-identity, attest-relay and snapshot-reorg
# activation parity, and the mirror bigint twin.
xchain-hub
# Block-hash conformance, the merkle and escrow-journal twins, rollback coverage.
xchain-sync
# Action-manifest, consensus-primitive, activation-constant and XCALL constants.
xchain-documentation
# The lint and metering vendored copies, consensus params, and the controller
# integration scenarios.
# +scripts: xchain-vm ships isolated-vm, a NATIVE addon, and this suite EXECUTES
# it rather than reading its source. The venue installs adjacent siblings with
# --ignore-scripts, which leaves no compiled binding and fails at load with
# "Cannot find module ./out/isolated_vm"; the marker gets it a scripts-running
# install, matching the explicit vm-dependency install step in ci.yml (XC-1520).
xchain-vm+scripts
# The action roundtrip golden, address-ref field conformance, the merkle twin.
xchain-sdk
# The decoder schema the integration scenarios build their fixtures from
# (XCHAIN_DECODER_SQL_PATH points straight at it when CI stages the schema repo).
xchain-decoder
# The merkle twin, the state-checkpoint fence parity, and the explorer launcher.
xchain-explorer
